`-Wextra` enables additional warnings that are not included in `-Wall`. These warnings are often useful but might be considered too pedantic or generate too many false positives for some codebases to be included in `-Wall`. For example, `-Wextra` often catches unused function parameters, uninitialized variables in specific contexts, or missing fallthrough comments in switch statements.
```c
void foo(int unused_param) { // -Wextra might warn 'unused_param' is unused
    // ...
}
```
